          "criterion": "AC-411-01",
          "result": "passed",
          "reference": "Golden create, grow, and rename scenarios produce exact claims only when a matching privileged process/file observation, complete size delta, time/path/operation match, and gap-free evidence agree. PID plus start time links the correct writer through authenticated ancestry to one task without leaking a reused PID. Incomplete privileged evidence becomes tool-linked only with a unique authenticated task; historical records become inferred; stream gaps, overlapping workspaces, and mismatched byte observations remain unknown. Each claim carries typed causal references, and the UI, export, and MCP presentation channels receive an identical evidence-bearing record."
        }
      ],
      "discovered_risks": [
        "Presentation parity is enforced through one shared immutable record; future channel-specific serializers must continue to consume it without modifying confidence, support, or limitations.",
        "Exact claims remain event-local and require live privileged evidence; historical metadata and FSEvents hints cannot be upgraded retrospectively.",
        "Workspace correlation is intentionally conservative: concurrent matching workspaces remain unknown even when that leaves useful activity unattributed."
